{ "code": "freight", "name": "Freight", "componentType": "Percentage", "value": 2.5 }

### 46. Compute opportunities — reuses the pricing comparison query, applies active cost components, persists top 10 cheapest
POST {{host}}/api/v1/procurement/requirements/{{createRequirement.response.body.$.data.id}}/opportunities
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 47. Get the persisted opportunity snapshot
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procurement/requirements/{{createRequirement.response.body.$.data.id}}/opportunities
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 48. My requirements
GET {{host}}/api/v1/procurement/requirements
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 49. Delete a requirement — cascades its opportunities
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/procurement/requirements/{{createRequirement.response.body.$.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- Notification ---
### Notifications are created by domain-event handlers only (welcome on register, alert on trigger) — there is no create endpoint.

### 50. My notifications
GET {{host}}/api/v1/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 51. Admin — all notifications, optionally filtered
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/notifications
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- Reporting ---

### 52. Request the weekly summary PDF — dates default to the last 7 days, language to Accept-Language
# @name requestReport
POST {{host}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: hi

{
  "reportType": "WeeklySummary",
  "format": "Pdf",
  "parameters": { "fromDate": "2026-09-20", "toDate": "2026-09-26", "language": "hi" }
}

### 52b. Request a price history CSV — Pro only (403 Report.ProRequired otherwise); mandiId optional
POST {{host}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reportType": "PriceHistory",
  "format": "Csv",
  "parameters": {
    "productId": "{{products.response.body.$.data[0].id}}",
    "fromDate": "2026-08-27",
    "toDate": "2026-09-26"
  }
}

### 53. Report status — Pending until the outbox dispatches GenerateReportHandler, then Ready/Failed
GET {{host}}/api/v1/reports/{{requestReport.response.body.$.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 53b. Download — the file once Ready; 409 Report.NotReady before that
GET {{host}}/api/v1/reports/{{requestReport.response.body.$.data.id}}/download
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 54. My reports — after 53b the downloaded report carries a lastDownloadedAtUtc
GET {{host}}/api/v1/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 55. Admin — all reports, optionally filtered
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/reports
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### --- Billing ---

### 56. Create a plan (admin)
# @name createPlan
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/billing/plans
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "pro-monthly", "name": "Pro Monthly", "price": 499, "currency": "INR", "billingPeriod": "Monthly" }

### 57. Active plans (mobile)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/billing/plans
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 58. Subscribe — charges via the stubbed payment gateway (always succeeds), creates the Subscription, flips SubscriptionTier to Pro
# @name subscribe
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/subscribe
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "planId": "{{createPlan.response.body.$.data.id}}" }

### 59. My subscription
GET {{host}}/api/v1/billing/subscription
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 60. Cancel my subscription
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/subscription/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 61. Admin — all subscriptions, optionally filtered
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/billing/subscriptions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 62. Admin — force-expire a subscription
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/billing/subscriptions/{{subscribe.response.body.$.data.id}}/expire
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 62a. Razorpay webhook (Development only — signature check is skipped). Returns 200 at once; the webhook inbox
### processor applies it within ~5 s (log: "Webhook … applied on attempt 1"), then GET /billing/subscription shows Active.
### Run it twice: the second call is a redelivery (same event id) — 200, nothing new queued.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
x-razorpay-event-id: evt_dev_{{subscribe.response.body.$.data.gatewayOrderId}}

{
  "entity": "event",
  "event": "payment.captured",
  "payload": {
    "payment": {
      "entity": { "id": "pay_dev_0001", "order_id": "{{subscribe.response.body.$.data.gatewayOrderId}}", "status": "captured",
                  "amount": {{subscribe.response.body.$.data.amountPaise}}, "currency": "INR" }
    }
  }
}

### 62b. Razorpay webhook for an unknown order — 200 now; the processor retries with backoff (30 s, 1 m, 2 m …) and parks it
### after WebhookInbox:MaxAttempts (log level Critical). Inspect: SELECT * FROM billing.webhook_inbox ORDER BY received_at_utc DESC;
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
x-razorpay-event-id: evt_dev_unknown_order_0001

{ "entity": "event", "event": "payment.captured", "payload": { "payment": { "entity": { "id": "pay_dev_0002", "order_id": "order_does_not_exist" } } } }

### 62c. Missing x-razorpay-event-id — 400 (ValidationProblemDetails), nothing stored
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/webhook
Content-Type: application/json

{ "entity": "event", "event": "payment.captured", "payload": {} }

### 62d. Razorpay webhook paying the wrong amount — 200 now; the processor parks it at once (Conflict
### Subscription.PaymentAmountMismatch, log level Critical) and the subscription stays PendingPayment.
### Run before 62a (or after a fresh subscribe); once 62a has run the subscription is already Active.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/billing/webhook
Content-Type: application/json
x-razorpay-event-id: evt_dev_wrong_amount_{{subscribe.response.body.$.data.gatewayOrderId}}

{ "entity": "event", "event": "payment.captured", "payload": { "payment": { "entity": { "id": "pay_dev_0003", "order_id": "{{subscribe.response.body.$.data.gatewayOrderId}}", "status": "captured", "amount": 100, "currency": "INR" } } } }

### 62e. Admin — webhook inbox, newest first. Filters: state=Pending|Processed|Parked, eventType=payment.captured
### After 62b/62d the parked ones show here; each park also raised an ops alert (Slack if OpsAlerts:SlackWebhookUrl is set,
### otherwise a Critical "OPS ALERT" log line). GET /health/ready answers "Degraded" (still 200) for 24 h after a park.
# @name parkedWebhooks
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/billing/webhooks?state=Parked
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 62f. Admin — one webhook with its raw payload and last error
GET {{host}}/api/v1/admin/billing/webhooks/{{parkedWebhooks.response.body.$.data[0].id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 62g. Admin — replay a parked webhook (204; 409 if it is not parked, 404 if unknown). The processor applies it within
### seconds; an order that still doesn't exist parks again after WebhookInbox:MaxAttempts.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/billing/webhooks/{{parkedWebhooks.response.body.$.data[0].id}}/replay
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 62h. Admin — send a test ops alert. 200 with "channel": "slack" once OpsAlerts:SlackWebhookUrl is set (check the
### Slack channel), "log" otherwise (a Critical "OPS ALERT" log line). 502 OpsAlerts.DeliveryFailed = Slack rejected it
### or was unreachable; the API log has Slack's reason (no_service = URL revoked/wrong, channel_is_archived, …).
POST {{host}}/api/v1/admin/notifications/ops-alerts/test
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

